#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) parallel whistler-Alfven wave test.
Hall-only: validates the Hall term of the generalized Ohm's law in normalized
CGS units (resistivity and electron-pressure-gradient terms disabled).

Parameters are chosen so that in CODE (normalized) units the ion scales are
O(1) and the ion cyclotron motion is resolved by the timestep:
  The geometry is in code units; the box is Lx = 6.4 d_i.
  Normalization: lNormSI = ion inertial length d_i, uNormSI = Alfven speed v_A,
  so that d_i ~ 1, v_A ~ 1, and (with q/(m c)=1 for the proton) B = Omega_i ~ 1.
  With dt = 0.02, dt*Omega_i = 0.02 << 1, so the Hall/whistler mode
  (bounded by Omega_i, since omega/Omega_i = (k d_i)^2 / (1+(k d_i)^2)) is
  numerically stable.  Physical inputs (n = 5 amu/cc, B = 5.22 nT,
  v_A ~ 51 km/s, d_i ~ 102 km) are solar-wind-like.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance instead.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Hall-only: resistive and electron-pressure-gradient terms are turned off
(both 0.0) to isolate the whistler dispersion.
#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Sub-cycle the B update: the explicit Hall advance is limited by the discrete
grid-scale modes, dt_sub < dx^2/(6 v_A d_i) ~ 1.7e-3 (dx = 0.1, v_A = d_i = 1),
so dt = 0.02 needs nHallSubcycle >= 12; 32 gives dt_sub = 6.25e-4 with margin.
#HALLSUBCYCLE
32                      nHallSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
5.2195e-9               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
1                       dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
0.5                     dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
6.25                    TimeMax

#RUN

#MOMENTTIMECENTERING
T                       useMomentTimeCentering

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB
